 way.\n\n**Does it support the valuation?** Only partly, and the evidence I found is thin.\n- The basket trades at a weighted forward P/E of 19x. Dividing 19x by 14% growth gives a PEG of about 1.4. That is reasonable for grid-equipment names but not cheap.\n- The growth looks concentrated. Two holdings drive most of the cited backlog conversion, and the next three (Braxen Cable, Ostrand Meters, Kelby Switchgear) are 24% of the fund together. If conversion slips at Voltaris or Tarnwell, the 14% figure is at risk.\n- These are long-duration growth names. The factsheet says a 50bp lower policy path historically lifts the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. Some of the 19x may therefore depend on rate expectations rather than earnings alone.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- I didn't check per-holding estimates.\n- I didn't look at the implied-volatility series (vltx_iv) or the realized-volatility series (vltx_rv).\n- I only found a single consensus figure, with no range of estimates.\n\nMy view is that 14% growth with rising estimates supports 19x. The margin of safety is modest, and the multiple is sensitive to rates and to execution at the top two holdings.\n\nSources: the `vltx-earnings-2027` and `vltx-factsheet` documents.","ttft_ms":4797,"type":"result","duration_ms":23951,"uuid":"9aaeb3e8-50bd-459c-8ce8-e5396535bf37","ttft_stream_ms":3900,"time_to_request_ms":62,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":12,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":70,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_